     "heading": "Expected shape",
     "html": "<ul><li>The skill refuses the plan and names the <strong>moat leak</strong> — the fatal error.</li><li>The <strong>alert-labelling</strong> produces the golden-case corpus. It fails the moat test (a competitor with the labelled dataset beats Barrier). It is <strong>Venture</strong>, not to be outsourced. Moat claim scored ≥ 0.5 and tagged.</li><li>The <strong>gas-safety rules and thresholds</strong> are the domain signal inside the guardrail engine. Buying a generic rules library either gives a commodity every rival can also license (no moat) or lets a vendor own the judgment that is the product. Keep the rules <strong>Venture</strong>; route the writing to <a class=\"skill-ref\" href=\"#/skill/guardrail-design\"><code>guardrail-design</code></a>.</li><li>The <strong>guardrail engine</strong> itself (the policy-enforcement machinery) is Platform — that part is fine to inherit.</li><li>Verdict <code>BOUNDARY WRONG — moat leak</code>; the one move: pull labelling and rules back in-venture; inherit the <em>engine</em>, not the <em>rules</em>.</li><li>Explicitly states the asymmetry: leaking the moat can end the venture, unlike the weeks lost to rebuilding a primitive.</li><li>Must NOT flatter &quot;good plan&quot;; must NOT accept &quot;we inherit everything&quot; when what is being inherited is the moat.</li></ul>"
